§ `Tests of ss 65 to 69`

§§ `s 65(1)(a) to (f): who is an appropriate person`
-- args: (a) specified; (b) case, is that fiduciary, is successor; (c) case, is a remaining fiduciary; (d) case, is the fiduciary; (e) case, is a survivor; (f) power to sign
-- (a)
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b) that person
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b) successor
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b) no longer-serving fiduciary, but neither that person nor a successor
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (b) the person is that fiduciary but the case does not arise
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c)
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (c) not a remaining fiduciary
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c) case does not arise
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (d)
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (d) not the fiduciary
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (d) case does not arise
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (e)
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (e) not a survivor
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (e) case does not arise
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (f)
#ASSERT `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- none
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- args: the eleven facts above, then the principal is described in (a) to (f), the principal may act through an agent or mandatary, the person is the authorized agent
-- (a)
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (f)
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (g) all three
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (g) principal is not described in (a) to (f)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- (g) principal may not act through an agent
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- (g) the person is not their agent
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- none
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 65(2) to (3): the time of signing; when an endorsement is made`
#ASSERT `the endorsement is authorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(2)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the endorsement is authorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(2)` FALSE)
